## atmospheric-pressure

atmospheric-pressure-ask = Will a syringe show the same air pressure as the barometer?
atmospheric-pressure-title = Measuring the atmospheric pressure with a syringe
atmospheric-pressure-choices = Less than the barometer
atmospheric-pressure-choices-2 = The same as the barometer
atmospheric-pressure-choices-3 = More than the barometer
atmospheric-pressure-air-label = The weather (air pressure)
atmospheric-pressure-air-options = A cyclone: 990 hPa
atmospheric-pressure-air-options-2 = An ordinary day: 1013 hPa
atmospheric-pressure-air-options-3 = An anticyclone: 1035 hPa
atmospheric-pressure-build-question = A 1 mL syringe, a dynamometer, a ruler and an aneroid barometer. We measure how long the syringe’s scale from 0 to 1 mL is and look at the barometer. First we pull the plunger out with the dynamometer with the nozzle open, then with the nozzle shut by a cap: to the 0.25, 0.5 and 1 mL marks. The force over the plunger’s area gives the air’s pressure. Will the syringe show the same pressure as the barometer?
atmospheric-pressure-setup = A 1 mL syringe with a cap for its nozzle, a dynamometer, a ruler, an aneroid barometer
